-- title:
--   Finite diamond action on L·ℚ(X₁(Mp)) fixing j, j(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the quotients $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $j, j_p \in K$ be elements whose Laurent series are, respectively, the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) and of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) (the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$, realised as the exponent-rescaling ring homomorphism) under the coefficient map. Let $K_2$ be the corresponding base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and assume $K_2 \le K$. Then there exist a type $G$ with a group structure, a finiteness witness, and a multiplicative semiring action of $G$ on $K$, such that: $G$ commutes with the $K_2$-algebra structure on $K$ given by the inclusion and `Algebra.IsInvariant K₂ K G` holds (every $G$-fixed element of $K$ comes from $K_2$); $G$ commutes with the $L$-action on $K$; and every $g \in G$ fixes both $j$ and $j_p$.
--
--   This is the field-theoretic form of the statement that the diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$ generate a finite group of automorphisms of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$, base changed to $L$, with invariant subfield that of $X_0(Mp)$, and that $j$ and $j(q^p)$ — being functions on $X_0(Mp)$ — are fixed. It supplies the Galois-descent input for the results on minimal primes over the $j$-chart of $X_1(Mp)$ that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_mulSemiringAction_isInvariant_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_smul_j_eq_x1_mul.lean

